in Muskogee County","/arc-plc/oklahoma/muskogee-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs from 1951 to 2025, 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids. On that middle, November to December came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those years, and in 2025 it ran 34% of normal. April to May is the wettest pair at 10.26 inches normal, and it ran 193% of normal in 2025. Grid 18440 had its driest year in 1963 at 45% of normal.</p>"}
